entry.summary:
Every value in my little embedded key-value store gets encrypted, then
This is mdc-lite, a ~348KB embeddable encrypted key-value store I
ModelDB,
Every put() call does this, in order:
Pack [key_len][key_bytes][value_bytes] into one plaintext buffer.
Encrypt the whole thing with XChaCha20-Poly1305 (a 256-bit key you
supply - the crate never generates or stores key material itself;
real key custody belongs to the platform's secure hardware, iOS
Secure Enclave or Android Keystore).
DNA-encode the resulting [nonce][ciphertext][tag] blob: 2 bits per
base, 00→A 01→C 10→G 11→T. Every byte maps to exactly 4 bases, so
there's no padding ambiguity on decode.
Write the ACGT text to disk, atomically (temp file + rename).
Filenames are keyed BLAKE3 hashes of the logical key, not the key name

rust
pub fn put(&self, key: &str, value: &[u8]) -> Result<(), LiteStoreError> {
    let mut plaintext = Vec::new();
    plaintext.extend_from_slice(&(key.len() as u16).to_le_bytes());
    plaintext.extend_from_slice(key.as_bytes());
    plaintext.extend_from_slice(value);

    let nonce = XChaCha20Poly1305::generate_nonce(&mut OsRng);
    let ciphertext = self.cipher().encrypt(&nonce, plaintext.as_ref())?;

    let mut record = nonce.to_vec();
    record.extend_from_slice(&ciphertext);
    let acgt_text = dna::encode(&record); // <- the actual bytes on disk

    fs::write(tmp_path, &acgt_text)?;
    fs::rename(tmp_path, final_path)?;
    Ok(())
}
